Against inter-sensor distance, the modeled magnetometer correlations followed the measured ones at << F.wr_cov_dist_d25_50_label >>~mm (<< F.rev_cov_dist_mag_d25_50_model_r >> against << F.rev_cov_dist_mag_d25_50_measured_r >>) and fell faster beyond, to << F.rev_cov_dist_mag_d200_225_model_r >> against << F.rev_cov_dist_mag_d200_225_measured_r >> at << F.wr_cov_dist_d200_225_label >>~mm (Fig.~\ref{fig:S3}D). Spatially correlated backgrounds did not change this, because the measured long-range correlation is a far-field pattern, not a cortical one. For the gradiometers, Fig.~\ref{fig:S3}E plots the median absolute correlation: << F.wr_cov_dist_grad_d25_50_model_abs_r >> in the model against << F.wr_cov_dist_grad_d25_50_measured_abs_r >> measured at << F.wr_cov_dist_d25_50_label >>~mm (median signed correlation << F.rev_cov_dist_grad_d25_50_model_r >> against << F.rev_cov_dist_grad_d25_50_measured_r >>). Their median signed correlations agreed at every distance.

